# Two host formals and four host own fields in one returned method; the two
# results keep their own captured values: 7834 and 1234. Exit 7 on the correct
# values; 81 is the program's own refusal.
fn: make2 (int: n; int: m) fn: () int
    int: a 1
    int: b 2
    int: third 3
    int: fourth 4
    fn: get () int
        return: n * 1000 + m * 100 + third * 10 + fourth
    return: get
@: first make2(7, 8)
@: second make2(1, 2)
int: got first()
int: got2 second()
int: ok 7
if: got != 7834 || got2 != 1234
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
